 and Resources News and Events Visit Campus Tri-Campus & South Bend Area Map and Directions Career Opportunities Campus Directory Admissions & Aid Enrollment Staff Apply to Holy Cross First Year Applicants International Applicants Transfer Applicants Financial Aid & Scholarships Types of Aid Loan Programs Student Employment Net Price Calculator Applying for Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Accounts Payment Plans Recursos en español Academics Faculty College Curriculum Majors and Minors Calendar, Catalog, and Schedule Study Abroad McKenna Library Moreau College Initiative Academic Support Transcript Requests Career Development Mathematics & Writing Centers Academic Accommodations Campus Life Student Activities Student Government Association Clubs & Organizations Residence Life What to Bring and Know Residence Information Apply for Residence Faith with Campus Ministry Chapel Schedule Theology on Tap Retreats and Pilgrimages Becoming Catholic Get Involved Student Wellness Student Handbook Dining Safety and Security Title IX and Sexual Assault Resources Technology Hammes Bookstore Current Students Faculty and Staff Athletics Search Scholar, Citizen, Leader, Disciple History and Mission Office of the President Leadership of the College Board of Trustees Holy Cross Presidents Accreditation News and Events Holy Cross Lecture Series Career Opportunities Join a community unlike any other Holy Cross College is a close-knit community of faculty and staff dedicated to preparing our students to become the scholars, citizens, leaders, and disciples the world needs now. The College maintains flexible workplace policies to promote a strong work-life balance culture for all employees, which include excellent healthcare, generous time-off, flexible hours, and remote work opportunities. If you share in our mission and are interested in joining one of the most distinctive environments in Catholic higher education, we welcome you to apply to any of the open positions listed below. Student Employment Student employment opportunities Current Faculty/Staff Openings Faculty/Staff career opportunities A few notes on submissions Only submissions to the posted positions will be considered—we do not maintain a database of resumes for future postings. Holy Cross College educates students with the competence to see and courage to act in the Catholic intellectual tradition. We value all students and employees and welcome the variety of experiences they bring. The College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, military status, genetic information, or age in the administration of any of its educational programs, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other school-administered programs, or in employment. Holy Cross College 54515 State Road 933 N. P.O. Box 308 Notre Dame, IN 46556 574-239-8377 About Admissions & Aid Academics Campus Life Campus Directory Apply to Holy Cross Visit Campus Map and Directions Facilities Rental McKenna Library Hammes Bookstore Career Opportunities The Congregation of Holy Cross is a community of Catholic, apostolic priests and brothers called by Jesus Christ and founded by Blessed Basil Moreau, who patterned the religious community after the Holy Family. LEARN MORE MEDIA INQUIRIES Please visit our media page for all inquiries. Copyright © 2025 Holy Cross College Notre Dame, Indiana"
