      "title": "Career Development",
      "description": "Career Development - Holy Cross VISIT APPLY ATHLETICS ALUMNI CURRENT STUDENTS ADMITTED STUDENTS FACULTY/STAFF × Holy Cross Website Search Visit Apply Give ABOUT HOLY CROSS ABOUT HOLY CROSS Scholar, Citizen, Leader, Disciple History and Mission Office of the President Leadership of the College Board of Trustees Holy Cross Presidents News and Events Academic Accreditation and Resources Visit Campus Tri-Campus & South Bend Area Map and Directions Career Opportunities Campus Directory ADMISSIONS & AID ADMISSIONS & AID Enrollment Programs Apply to Holy Cross First Year Applicants International Applicants Transfer Applicants Enrollment Staff Financial Aid & Scholarships Types of Aid Loan Programs Student Employment Net Price Calculator Applying for Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Accounts Payment Plans Recursos en español ACADEMICS ACADEMICS Faculty College Curriculum Majors and Minors Calendar, Catalog, and Schedule Study Abroad McKenna Library Moreau College Initiative Academic Support Transcript Requests Career Development Mathematics & Writing Centers Academic Accommodations NEWS & EVENTS Holy Cross College, Notre Dame Establish New Pathway for Student Veterans Holy Cross College Offers Parking for AC/DC Concert and Notre Dame Football Games Welcome Weekend Gives Way to a New Year at Holy Cross College CAMPUS LIFE CAMPUS LIFE Student Activities Student Government Association Clubs & Organizations Residence Life What to Bring and Know Residence Information Apply for Residence Faith with Campus Ministry Chapel Schedule Theology on Tap Retreats and Pilgrimages Becoming Catholic Get Involved Student Wellness Student Handbook Dining Safety and Security Title IX and Sexual Assault Resources Technology Current Students Faculty and Staff Athletics Visit Apply Give About Holy Cross Scholar, Citizen, Leader, Disciple History and Mission Office of the President Leadership of the College Board of Trustees Holy Cross Presidents Academic Accreditation and Resources News and Events Visit Campus Tri-Campus & South Bend Area Map and Directions Career Opportunities Campus Directory Admissions & Aid Enrollment Staff Apply to Holy Cross First Year Applicants International Applicants Transfer Applicants Financial Aid & Scholarships Types of Aid Loan Programs Student Employment Net Price Calculator Applying for Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Accounts Payment Plans Recursos en español Academics Faculty College Curriculum Majors and Minors Calendar, Catalog, and Schedule Study Abroad McKenna Library Moreau College Initiative Academic Support Transcript Requests Career Development Mathematics & Writing Centers Academic Accommodations Campus Life Student Activities Student Government Association Clubs & Organizations Residence Life What to Bring and Know Residence Information Apply for Residence Faith with Campus Ministry Chapel Schedule Theology on Tap Retreats and Pilgrimages Becoming Catholic Get Involved Student Wellness Student Handbook Dining Safety and Security Title IX and Sexual Assault Resources Technology Hammes Bookstore Current Students Faculty and Staff Athletics Search Campus Life Student Activities Student Gov Association Clubs and Organizations Residence Life Apply for Residence What to Bring and Know Residence Information Faith with Campus Ministry Chapel Schedule Theology on Tap Retreats & Pilgrimages Becoming Catholic Get Involved Student Wellness Student Handbook Dining Safety & Security Technology Title IX Incident Report Hammes Bookstore Career Development Career Development: Preparing courageous leaders The goal of career development at Holy Cross College is to help students understand how their growth as a scholar, citizen, leader, and disciple is transferable to the skills necessary to find success in their endeavors after graduation. Every student will be personally and individually helped by a team member of the Office of Student Success. No matter where you are in your career development journey, you’ll have access to a wide range of resources and experiences, including: One-on-one Mentoring from an experienced team member willing to help you build a resume, make connections to grow your network, or find an opportunity to gain hands-on, practical work experience needed to discern and prepare for your next opportunity. Pathway U, which helps students examine their skills, values, and work style preferences to discover possible career pathways and map the skills and knowledge needed to be successful in each field. Handshake, where both Fortune 500 companies and local employers alike post full and part-time job openings, internships, volunteer opportunities, post-graduate service positions, and fellowships. Professional Internships (every student earning a bachelor’s degree completes at least one), where you can test out your career path, experience new work environments, and build your professional network. Ascend Indiana, which pairs students with an Indiana-based career mentor to help introduce students to early career positions (0 – 3-years’ experience) with partner organizations/companies based throughout the state of Indiana. Engage in conversation with potential employers during our annual Career Fair , a highly curated event featuring employers hand-picked by our staff. Hear from Holy Cross alumni living and working in the area as they share their professional experiences at on-campus events. Senior Capstone, a course to help students understand and share how their passions and skills can make an impact in their first post-graduate opportunity. Meet your professional mentors Wendy Chapman, Career Development 574-239-8309 [email protected] Mailing address: Holy Cross College Career Development P.O. Box 308 Notre Dame, IN 46556-0308 Holy Cross College 54515 State Road 933 N. P.O. Box 308 Notre Dame, IN 46556 574-239-8377 About Admissions & Aid Academics Campus Life Campus Directory Apply to Holy Cross Visit Campus Map and Directions Facilities Rental McKenna Library Hammes Bookstore Career Opportunities The Congregation of Holy Cross is a community of Catholic, apostolic priests and brothers called by Jesus Christ and founded by Blessed Basil Moreau, who patterned the religious community after the Holy Family. LEARN MORE MEDIA INQUIRIES Please visit our media page for all inquiries. Copyright © 2025 Holy Cross College Notre Dame, Indiana"
    },
